[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Open Games (1...e5)"]
[Variation "Ruy Lopez: Closed"]
[ECO "C84"]
[Character "solid,positional"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "queenside-space,central-pawns"]
[For "black"]
[Kind "main"]
[Opponent "3.Bb5"]
[Start "giuoco-piano 2...Nc6"]

3. Bb5 { Attacks the knight that defends e5. The threat is slow, so Black has time to ask the bishop a question. } 3... a6 { Asks the bishop to decide. If it takes on c6, Black gets two bishops; if it retreats, ...b5 gains space. } 4. Ba4 ( 4. Bxc6 dxc6 { The recapture opens the bishop on c8 and gives Black two bishops. } 5. O-O ( 5. d3 f6 6. Nbd2 c5 ) ( 5. Nxe5 Qd4 { Attacks the knight on e5 and the pawn on e4 at once, so Black wins the pawn back. } 6. Nf3 ( 6. Nd3 Qxe4+ 7. Qe2 Bf5 ) ( 6. Qh5 g6 { Hits the queen, and the knight on e5 is still attacked. } ) 6... Qxe4+ 7. Qe2 Qxe2+ 8. Kxe2 Bd7 { Black has the two bishops in an open position and White's king has lost the right to castle. Plan: ...O-O-O and ...Re8. } ) ( 5. Nc3 f6 6. d4 exd4 7. Qxd4 Qxd4 8. Nxd4 Bd7 ) ( 5. d4 exd4 6. Qxd4 Qxd4 7. Nxd4 Bd7 { With queens off, the two bishops count for more. Plan: ...O-O-O and ...c5 to chase the knight. } ) ( 5. h3 f6 ) 5... f6 { Defends e5 with a pawn and keeps the bishops free. } 6. d4 exd4 7. Nxd4 c5 { Hits the knight, and after it moves Black trades queens and keeps the bishop pair. } 8. Nb3 Qxd1 9. Rxd1 Bg4 ) 4... Nf6 { Develops and attacks e4, so White must decide how to defend it. } 5. O-O ( 5. Nc3 Be7 6. O-O b5 7. Bb3 d6 ) ( 5. d3 d6 { Gives e5 a pawn defender and frees the c8 bishop. } 6. c3 Be7 7. O-O O-O ) 5... Be7 { Develops the bishop and prepares to castle. } 6. Re1 b5 { Gains space and asks the bishop to leave the long diagonal. If it takes on c6, Black recaptures. } 7. Bb3 d6 { Gives e5 a pawn defender and frees the c8 bishop. } 8. c3 O-O { Castle: the king is safe and the rook can join the centre. } 9. h3 Nb8 { The knight on c6 does little, so it heads back via b8 to d7, where it supports e5 and the centre. } 10. d4 Nbd7 11. Nbd2 Bb7 { Puts the last minor piece on the long diagonal, aimed at e4. } 12. Bc2 Re8 { Backs up the e5 pawn. Plan: ...Bf8 and ...c5 or ...exd4 to break open the centre. If White plays d5, keep the position closed with ...c6. } *
